{
  "name": "Pancreatic Cancer",
  "gmf_version": 2,
  "remarks": [
    "Pancreatic adenocarcinoma: age-shaped incidence, symptomatic/incidental",
    "presentation, diagnostic workup, NCCN resectability-based treatment",
    "(resectable / borderline resectable / locally advanced / metastatic),",
    "gemcitabine chemotherapy, surveillance, recurrence and terminal decline.",
    "",
    "ENCOUNTER DISCIPLINE: ModSynthea gives each person a single encounter",
    "reservation (State.java Encounter/EncounterEnd). Every Encounter opened",
    "here reaches an EncounterEnd before any Delay >= 1 day or Guard, and",
    "every such Delay sits between an EncounterEnd and the next Encounter.",
    "The only Delays inside an open encounter are Postoperative_Stay (Whipple",
    "length of stay) and Hospice_Stay (hospice benefit period), both far",
    "under the linter's 90-day warning threshold. The pre-fix module opened",
    "Staging_Workup and then ran Determine_Resectability straight into",
    "months-to-years of Postoperative_Recovery / Reassessment_After_Neoadjuvant",
    "/ Supportive_Care with that encounter still open -- three CRITICAL",
    "encounter-lock findings. All chemotherapy is now closed per-cycle",
    "encounters (open -> administer -> close -> inter-cycle Delay), surgery",
    "is a bounded inpatient admission, and terminal decline is a closed",
    "hospice-visit loop ending in Death recorded outside any open encounter.",
    "",
    "INCIDENCE: the pre-fix module rolled a single 0.00013 chance at exactly",
    "age 50 (~100x under SEER and spiked at one age). Replaced with an",
    "annual age-banded reroll from 45: 5e-5/yr (45-54), 1.5e-4/yr (55-64),",
    "3e-4/yr (65+). Cumulative to age 90 = 10(5e-5) + 10(1.5e-4) + 25(3e-4)",
    "= 0.95%, ~1.25% to age 100 -- below SEER's cited ~1.7% lifetime risk",
    "(SEER Cancer Stat Facts: Pancreatic Cancer,",
    "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/pancreas.html) because SEER's",
    "figure integrates rates that keep climbing past age 70 (peak incidence",
    "~40-50/100,000/yr in the 70s-80s) more steeply than this three-band",
    "approximation; the brief-specified bands are used as given rather than",
    "re-solved to hit 1.7% exactly. Onset is spread across ages 45+, not",
    "spiked at one age.",
    "",
    "GEMCITABINE: every dose is now a clinician-administered infusion",
    "(administration: true), routed to a professional/outpatient claim line",
    "via rxnorm_hcpcs_map (RxNorm 1719003 -> HCPCS J9201). Administration",
    "rows cannot stack in ModSynthea (verified in prior remediation tasks),",
    "so no MedicationEnd is needed; the pre-fix module's single open-ended",
    "MedicationOrder (no administration flag, no MedicationEnd, no course",
    "length) is gone from every arm.",
    "",
    "TREATMENT COURSES (NCCN Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma Guideline categories",
    "match this module's pre-existing pancreatic_stage values):",
    "- Resectable (15%): upfront pancreaticoduodenectomy (Whipple), then 6",
    "  cycles adjuvant gemcitabine (CONKO-001, Oettle et al. JAMA",
    "  2013;310:1473 -- 6 months adjuvant gemcitabine, median OS 22.8mo).",
    "- Borderline resectable (25%): 3 cycles neoadjuvant gemcitabine,",
    "  restaging, resection, then 3 more cycles adjuvant (6 total, split",
    "  around surgery -- PREOPANC, Versteijne et al. J Clin Oncol",
    "  2020;38:1763).",
    "- Locally advanced / unresectable (40%): 6 cycles induction gemcitabine",
    "  then palliative-care integration and hospice (LAP07, Hammel et al.",
    "  JAMA 2016;315:1844 -- chemo alone median OS ~13mo in this population).",
    "- Metastatic (20%): palliative-care referral at diagnosis, 4 cycles",
    "  gemcitabine (Burris et al. J Clin Oncol 1997;15:2403 -- single-agent",
    "  gemcitabine median OS 5.65mo), then hospice.",
    "",
    "the former shared 'cancer_stage' attribute (also written by",
    "ovarian_cancer.json under a different value set: resectable/",
    "borderline/locally_advanced/metastatic here vs. I/II/III/IV there) was",
    "renamed to 'pancreatic_stage' by the cross-module attribute-rename task",
    "-- verified by grep that no other module reads it.",
    "",
    "SECOND ROOT CAUSE OF THE UNDER-COUNT (found during this task's own",
    "verification, not named in the audit): the module's six Symptom states",
    "(Jaundice/Dark_Urine/Pruritus/Abdominal_Pain/Weight_Loss/Anorexia) had",
    "'codes' but no top-level 'symptom' field. State$Symptom.process calls",
    "Person.setSymptom(module, cause, symptom, ...), which does",
    "symptoms.containsKey(type) on a ConcurrentHashMap -- with symptom",
    "deserialized null, this throws NullPointerException the instant",
    "generatePerson() first reached one of these states, discarding that",
    "person's entire in-progress record (including any ConditionOnset from",
    "a few states earlier) before it could ever reach the CSV export.",
    "90% of onsets route through Jaundice_Presentation or",
    "Abdominal_Pain_Presentation (Determine_Presentation_Type: 0.7/0.2),",
    "so this alone was enough to explain a smoke run showing zero cases",
    "against a nonzero calibrated hazard. Confirmed by an isolated in-memory",
    "harness (TestHelper.exportOff() + Generator, no CSV/FHIR writes): 1500",
    "people, 33775 Cancer_Incidence_Check rolls, expected 5.15 onsets by the",
    "bands above, 0 recorded (Poisson P(X=0)=0.6%) before the fix; every",
    "Symptom state now carries 'symptom' (Person.setSymptom's map key) and",
    "an 'exact' severity, matching the working convention used by",
    "pneumonia.json/valvular_heart_failure.json/mantle_cell_lymphoma.json."
  ],
  "states": {
    "Initial": {
      "type": "Initial",
      "direct_transition": "Age_Check"
    },
    "Age_Check": {
      "type": "Guard",
      "allow": {
        "condition_type": "Age",
        "operator": ">=",
        "quantity": 45,
        "unit": "years"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Cancer_Incidence_Check"
    },
    "Cancer_Incidence_Check": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "Age-banded annual incidence (brief-specified bands): 5e-5/yr 45-54,",
        "1.5e-4/yr 55-64, 3e-4/yr 65+. Evaluated oldest-first because",
        "ComplexTransition.follow takes the first condition that is true.",
        "See module header for the cumulative-risk arithmetic and SEER",
        "citation."
      ],
      "complex_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": ">=",
            "quantity": 65,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "distributions": [
            {
              "transition": "Pancreatic_Cancer_Onset",
              "distribution": 0.0003
            },
            {
              "transition": "Annual_Reroll_Delay",
              "distribution": 0.9997
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "Age",
            "operator": ">=",
            "quantity": 55,
            "unit": "years"
          },
          "distributions": [
            {
              "transition": "Pancreatic_Cancer_Onset",
              "distribution": 0.00015
            },
            {
              "transition": "Annual_Reroll_Delay",
              "distribution": 0.99985
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "distributions": [
            {
              "transition": "Pancreatic_Cancer_Onset",
              "distribution": 5e-05
            },
            {
              "transition": "Annual_Reroll_Delay",
              "distribution": 0.99995
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "Annual_Reroll_Delay": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "remarks": [
        "Pure annual incidence reroll; no screening test exists for average-",
        "risk pancreatic cancer (no USPSTF recommendation), so this loop",
        "generates no health-record activity until onset."
      ],
      "range": {
        "low": 11,
        "high": 13,
        "unit": "months"
      },
      "direct_transition": "Cancer_Incidence_Check"
    },
